y <MATH_0003> of formal\nobjects of  <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is the category with the following objects and\nmorphisms.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>formal object <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nconsists of an object <MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008>, and a collection\nindexed by <MATH_0009> of objects <MATH_0010> of\n<MATH_0011> and morphisms\n<MATH_0012> lying over the projection\n<MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0003> Let <MATH_0014> and <MATH_0015> be\nformal objects of <MATH_0016>.  A <TEXTITOPEN_0003>morphism <MATH_0017> of\nformal objects<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> consists of a map <MATH_0018> in\n<MATH_0019> and a collection <MATH_0020>\nof morphisms of <MATH_0021> lying over\n<MATH_0022>,\nsuch that for every <MATH_0023> the diagram\n<MATH_0024>\ncommutes.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e925246759fc79e99ed24879a69fc09f6499b6bcd8c02d0100406db96b2549da", "unit_id": "tag:06H3:statement"}
